/-
# BMAX — Bender 1970, 1.7(i): `F_π(B) ≤ A` (Bender 1981, Lemma 2.3(i))

Target (verbatim from the brief):

`Work.BMAX.Bender17i :` for a finite simple `G`, a coatomic (= maximal) subgroup `A`,
`B ≠ ⊤`, `A ⇝ B` (`Work.GW2.BRel`) and `F*(A)` *not* a `p`-group for any prime `p`,

  `F_π(B) ≤ A`,  where `π = π(F(A))` = `primesOf (fittingIn A)`.

This is Bender 1981, Lemma 2.3(i), quoted there from Bender 1970 §1.7.  The exception `hnot`
("unless `F*(Ĥ)` is a `p`-group") is essential *in this workspace's vocabulary*: `layer` is the
join of the **normal** quasisimple subgroups whereas Bender's `E(X)` is generated by the
components, so `F*(X)` can be `⊥` while `E(X) ≠ 1`; then `BRel A B` becomes vacuous and
`F_π(B) ≤ A` fails (explicit `A₁₀` counterexample recorded in `Bender17Prime.lean`).  Since `⊥`
*is* a `p`-group for every prime `p`, `hnot` excludes exactly that degeneration.

## Proof structure

Let `X ≤ F(A)` be a witness of `A ⇝ B`, i.e. `N_{F*(A)}(X) ≤ B`.

* **Step 1: `F*(A) ≤ B`** (proved here).
  `hnot` forces `F(A)` to be a Dedekind group — every subgroup of `F(A)` is normal in `F(A)`;
  this is the area's `Work.BMAX.Bender17i_fitting_dedekind_hnot`.  Hence `F(A) ≤ N(X)`; and
  `layer(A) ≤ C(F(A))` centralizes `F(A) ⊇ X`, so it also normalizes `X`
  (`Work.BMAX.LayerCentralizesFitting`).  Therefore
  `F*(A) = F(A) ⊔ layer(A) ≤ N(X) ⊓ F*(A) ≤ B`.
* **Step 2: `F*(A) ≤ B` + `hnot` ⇒ `F_π(B) ≤ A`** (proved in the sibling file
  `Submission.Work.BMAX.Bender17i_of_fstar_le`, `Work.BMAX.Bender17i_of_fstar_le`).
  Concretely: for `q ∈ π = π(F(A))`, the subgroup `R := O^q(F*(A))` is non-trivial (`hnot`),
  lies in `A` and is normalised by `A`, so `N_G(R) = A` (maximality of `A` + simplicity of `G`);
  Bender 1970, 1.7(ii) — `⁅O_q(B), O^q(F*(A))⁆ = ⊥`, the Thompson `P × K` step — gives
  `O_q(B) ≤ C_G(R) ≤ N_G(R) = A`, and `F_π(B) = ⨆_{q ∈ π} O_q(B)`.

This file proves Step 1 and assembles the two steps.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.BMAX.Defs
import Submission.Work.BMAX.Basic
import Submission.Work.BMAX.D17Defs
import Submission.Work.BMAX.LayerCentralizesFitting
import Submission.Work.BMAX.BRel_witness_facts
import Submission.Work.BMAX.Bender17i_of_fstar_le
import Submission.Work.BMAX.centralizer_pResidualIn_witness_le
import Submission.Work.BMAX.inf_fittingIn_le_pCoreIn_of_le_pCoreIn
import Submission.Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_inf_pResidualIn_fittingIn_eq_bot
import Submission.Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_commutator_pCoreIn
import Submission.Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_zcenterIn_fittingIn_ne_bot
import Submission.Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn_zcenterIn_fittingIn
import Submission.Work.BMAX.fstarIn_le_pResidualIn_of_notMem_primesOf
import Submission.Work.BMAX.pResidualIn_fstarIn_eq_sup
import Submission.Work.BMAX.fittingPiIn_le_iSup_pCoreIn

set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace Work.BMAX

open Subgroup

/-- `F_π(K) ≤ K`: `fittingPiIn π K` is a double image under subtype maps. -/
theorem bender17i_fittingPiIn_le_self {G : Type*} [Group G] (π : Set ℕ) (K : Subgroup G) :
    Work.GW2.fittingPiIn π K ≤ K := by
  rw [Work.GW2.fittingPiIn]
  exact Subgroup.map_subtype_le _

/-- `F*(K) ≤ K`: `fstarIn K` is the image of `fstar K` under `K.subtype`. -/
theorem bender17i_fstarIn_le_self {G : Type*} [Group G] (K : Subgroup G) :
    Work.GW2.fstarIn K ≤ K := by
  rw [Work.GW2.fstarIn]
  exact Subgroup.map_subtype_le _

/-- **Step 1 of Bender 1970, 1.7(i), conditional on Dedekind-ness of `F(A)`.**  If every subgroup
of `F(A)` is normal in `F(A)`, then the relation `A ⇝ B` forces `F*(A) ≤ B`: the witness
`X ≤ F(A)` is normalised by `F(A)`, and `E(A)` centralises `F(A) ⊇ X`
(`Work.BMAX.LayerCentralizesFitting`), hence normalises `X` too.

(The unconditional statement `hnot ⟹ F(A)` Dedekind is the area's open auxiliary
`Work.BMAX.Bender17i_fitting_dedekind_hnot`; the *main* theorem below no longer needs it.) -/
theorem bender17i_step_fstar_le_of_dedekind (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (hG : IsSimpleGroup G)
    (A B : Subgroup G) (hA : IsCoatom A) (hrel : Work.GW2.BRel A B)
    (hded : ∀ X : Subgroup G, X ≤ Work.GW2.fittingIn A →
      Work.GW2.fittingIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G)) :
    Work.GW2.fstarIn A ≤ B := by
  obtain ⟨X, hX, hXB⟩ := hrel
  have hN : Work.GW2.fittingIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) := hded X hX
  have hstar : Work.GW2.fstarIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) := by
    rw [Work.GW2.fstarIn_eq_sup]
    refine sup_le hN ?_
    refine le_trans (LayerCentralizesFitting G A) ?_
    rw [Subgroup.le_normalizer_iff]
    intro l hl x hx
    rw [Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff] at hl
    have hlx : l * x * l⁻¹ = x := by rw [← hl x (hX hx)]; group
    rw [hlx]; exact hx
  exact le_trans (le_inf hstar le_rfl) hXB

/-! **Bender 1970, 1.7(i)** is assembled at the end of this file from the general `hD` below
(`bender17i_of_hD`), with Bender's own Thompson argument run on the *witness*
`S = N_{F*(A)}(X)` of the relation `A ⇝ B` in place of `F*(A)`; no Dedekind-ness of `F(A)` is
needed. -/

/-! ## The case `E(A) = ⊥`: Bender 17(i) without the Dedekind auxiliary

The reduction `Bender17i ⇐ (F(A) is Dedekind)` above is *not* the only route to 1.7(i): Bender's
own proof of 1.7 uses the Thompson `P × K` lemma (his 1.1) with the **witness** `S = N_{F*(A)}(X)`
of the relation `A ⇝ B` in place of `F*(A)`, and only needs `F(A)` to be Dedekind in order to
*upgrade* `O^q(S)` to `O^q(F*(A))`.  In the case `E(A) = E = ⊥` (so `F*(A) = F(A)`) that upgrade
is unnecessary and the argument goes through directly:

* `O_q(B) ⊓ A` is a `q`-subgroup of `A` lying in `O_q(B)`, hence `O_q(B) ⊓ A ≤ O_q(A)`
  (`inf_fittingIn_le_pCoreIn_of_le_pCoreIn`);
* for a `q'`-element `x` of `S ⊆ F*(A) = F(A)` one gets
  `⁅O_q(B) ⊓ A, x⁆ ≤ O_q(A) ⊓ O^q(F(A)) = ⊥`
  (`pCoreIn_inf_pResidualIn_fittingIn_eq_bot`) — this is the step `hD` below;
* Thompson's lemma with `P = O_q(Z(F(A))) ⊢ O_q(B)` finishes, giving `⁅O_q(B), O^q(S)⁆ = ⊥`;
* `O_q(B)` therefore centralises `O^q(Z(F(A)))`, which is a non-trivial normal subgroup of the
  coatom `A`, so `O_q(B) ≤ A`.

The last step is where this route is *strictly* better than the Dedekind one: it only needs the
`q`-core of `Z(F(A))` to be non-trivial (true by `hnot`), not the full Dedekind-ness of `F(A)`.
-/

/-- `Z(F(A)) ≤ C_G(S)` whenever `S ≤ F*(A)`: the centre of the Fitting subgroup centralises
`F(A)` and (by `LayerCentralizesFitting`) is centralised by the layer, and `F*(A) = F(A) ⊔ E(A)`
is generated by the two. -/
theorem bender17i_zcenterIn_le_centralizer {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] {A S : Subgroup G}
    (hS : S ≤ Work.GW2.fstarIn A) :
    Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤ Subgroup.centralizer (S : Set G) := by
  have hZ : Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤
      Subgroup.centralizer ((Work.GW2.fstarIn A : Subgroup G) : Set G) := by
    rw [Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff, Work.GW2.fstarIn_eq_sup]
    refine sup_le ?_ ?_
    · rw [Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff]
      intro z hz
      rw [Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff]
      intro f hf
      exact ((Work.GW2.mem_zcenterIn.mp hz).2 f hf).symm
    · intro e he
      rw [Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff]
      intro z hz
      exact Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp (LayerCentralizesFitting G A he) z
        (Work.GW2.mem_zcenterIn.mp hz).1
  exact le_trans hZ (Subgroup.centralizer_le (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hS))

/-- If `y` commutes with `x`, it commutes with every element of the cyclic subgroup `⟨x⟩`. -/
theorem bender17i_commute_zpowers_of_commute {G : Type*} [Group G] {x y : G}
    (h : y * x = x * y) {k : G} (hk : k ∈ Subgroup.zpowers x) : y * k = k * y := by
  have hx : x ∈ Subgroup.centralizer ({y} : Set G) := by
    rw [Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff]
    intro z hz
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hz
    subst hz
    exact h
  exact (Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp ((Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hx) hk)) y (Set.mem_singleton y)

/-- **Thompson's `P × K` step of Bender 1970, 1.7 (ii)** in the form needed here: if
`N₀ := O_q(Z(F(A)))` lies in `B`, centralises `S`, and has `C_G(N₀) ≤ A`, then from
`⁅O_q(B) ⊓ A, O^q(S)⁆ = ⊥` one gets `⁅O_q(B), O^q(S)⁆ = ⊥`.

For each `q'`-element `x ∈ S`, Thompson's lemma is applied to the action of `N₀ × ⟨x⟩` on the
`q`-group `O_q(B) ◁ B`: the actors commute (`N₀ ≤ C_G(S)`), and the `N₀`-fixed points of
`O_q(B)` lie in `C_G(N₀) ≤ A`, hence in `O_q(B) ⊓ A`, and are therefore fixed by `x`. -/
theorem bender17i_commutator_of_coatom_facts {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G]
    (A B S : Subgroup G) (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime)
    (hN₀B : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤ B)
    (hN₀S : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤
      Subgroup.centralizer (S : Set G))
    (hcent : Subgroup.centralizer
      ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) : Subgroup G) : Set G) ≤ A)
    (hSB : S ≤ B)
    (hD : ⁅Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A, Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S⁆ = ⊥) :
    ⁅Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B, Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S⁆ = ⊥ := by
  classical
  haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
  set N₀ : Subgroup G :=
    Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) with hN₀def
  rw [Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer]
  refine (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff (H := Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B)
    (K := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S)).mpr ?_
  rw [Work.BMAX.pResidualIn]
  refine (Subgroup.closure_le (K := Subgroup.centralizer
    ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B : Subgroup G) : Set G))).mpr ?_
  rintro x ⟨hxS, hxq⟩
  have hKc : ¬ q ∣ Nat.card ↥(Subgroup.zpowers x) := by
    rw [Nat.card_zpowers]
    exact hxq
  have hcomm : ∀ y ∈ N₀, ∀ k ∈ Subgroup.zpowers x, y * k = k * y := by
    intro y hy k hk
    have hyx : y * x = x * y :=
      ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp (hN₀S hy)) x hxS).symm
    exact bender17i_commute_zpowers_of_commute hyx hk
  have hfix : ∀ v ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B,
      (∀ y ∈ N₀, v * y = y * v) → ∀ k ∈ Subgroup.zpowers x, v * k = k * v := by
    intro v hv hvN k hk
    have hvC : v ∈ Subgroup.centralizer (N₀ : Set G) := by
      rw [Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff]
      intro y hy
      exact (hvN y hy).symm
    have hvA : v ∈ A := hcent hvC
    have hvD : v ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A := Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hv, hvA⟩
    have hxW : x ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.subset_closure hxS hxq
    have hvx : v * x = x * v := by
      have hmem := (Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer.mp hD) hvD
      exact ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp hmem) x hxW).symm
    exact bender17i_commute_zpowers_of_commute hvx hk
  have hPK := Work.BMAX.pcpc_thompson_PK_commutator (p := q) (B := B)
    (Q := Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B) (P := N₀) (K := Subgroup.zpowers x)
    (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q B) hN₀B (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr (hSB hxS))
    (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn B q) (Work.BMAX.pcpc_isPGroup_pCoreIn q B)
    (Work.BMAX.pcpc_isPGroup_pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)))
    hKc hcomm hfix
  have hC : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤
      Subgroup.centralizer ((Subgroup.zpowers x : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
    Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer.mp hPK
  refine Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mpr ?_
  intro v hv
  exact ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp (hC hv)) x (Subgroup.mem_zpowers x)).symm

/-- **The step `hD` of the `E(A) = ⊥` case**: `O_q(B) ⊓ A` commutes with `O^q(S)`.

Since `S ≤ F*(A) = F(A)` here, a `q'`-element `x ∈ S` lies in `O^q(F(A))`, and for
`v ∈ O_q(B) ⊓ A` the commutator `⁅v, x⁆` lies both in `O_q(A)`
(`inf_fittingIn_le_pCoreIn_of_le_pCoreIn`, as `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ (O_q(B) ⊓ A) ⊓ F(A)`) and in
`O^q(F(A))`, hence is trivial (`pCoreIn_inf_pResidualIn_fittingIn_eq_bot`). -/
theorem bender17i_hD_of_layerIn_eq_bot {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] {A B S : Subgroup G}
    (hSB : S ≤ B) (hSf : S ≤ Work.GW2.fstarIn A) (hL : Work.GW2.layerIn A = ⊥)
    (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime) :
    ⁅Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A, Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S⁆ = ⊥ := by
  classical
  haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
  -- `S ≤ F(A)` in the layerless case
  have hSF : S ≤ Work.GW2.fittingIn A := by
    rw [Work.GW2.fstarIn_eq_sup, hL, sup_bot_eq] at hSf
    exact hSf
  rw [Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer]
  refine (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff (H := Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A)
    (K := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S)).mpr ?_
  rw [Work.BMAX.pResidualIn]
  refine (Subgroup.closure_le (K := Subgroup.centralizer
    (((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A : Subgroup G)) : Set G))).mpr ?_
  rintro x ⟨hxS, hxq⟩
  have hxF : x ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A := hSF hxS
  have hxA : x ∈ A := Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_self A hxF
  have hxB : x ∈ B := hSB hxS
  have hxR : x ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
    Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.subset_closure hxF hxq
  refine Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mpr ?_
  intro v hv
  obtain ⟨hvQ, hvA⟩ := Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hv
  -- `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ O_q(B)`
  have hconjQ : x * v * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B :=
    (Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn B q hxB) v).mp hvQ
  have hxinvQ : x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B := by
    have h := (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B).inv_mem hconjQ
    rwa [show (x * v * x⁻¹)⁻¹ = x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ from by group] at h
  have hcomQ : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B := by
    have h := (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B).mul_mem hvQ hxinvQ
    rwa [show v * (x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹) = v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ from by group] at h
  -- `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ A` and `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ F(A)`
  have hcomA : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ A :=
    A.mul_mem (A.mul_mem (A.mul_mem hvA hxA) (A.inv_mem hvA)) (A.inv_mem hxA)
  have hconjF : v * x * v⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A :=
    (Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A hvA) x).mp hxF
  have hcomF : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A :=
    (Work.GW2.fittingIn A).mul_mem hconjF ((Work.GW2.fittingIn A).inv_mem hxF)
  -- hence `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ O_q(A)`
  have hsub : (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A) ⊓ Work.GW2.fittingIn A ≤ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q A :=
    Work.BMAX.inf_fittingIn_le_pCoreIn_of_le_pCoreIn A B (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A) q hq
      inf_le_left inf_le_right
  have hOqA : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q A :=
    hsub (Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hcomQ, hcomA⟩, hcomF⟩)
  -- and `⁅v, x⁆ ∈ O^q(F(A))`
  have hAR : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer
      ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
    Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pResidualIn_of_le_normalizer (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A)
  have hOqR : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
    (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).mul_mem
      ((Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (hAR hvA) x).mp hxR)
      ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).inv_mem hxR)
  -- so it is trivial
  have hbot : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ = 1 := by
    have hinf : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q A ⊓
        Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) = ⊥ :=
      Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_inf_pResidualIn_fittingIn_eq_bot A q hq
    have : v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup G) := by
      rw [← hinf]
      exact Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hOqA, hOqR⟩
    exact Subgroup.mem_bot.mp this
  calc v * x = (v * x * v⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * (x * v) := by group
    _ = x * v := by rw [hbot, one_mul]

/-- `C_G(O_q(Z(F(A)))) ≤ A` for a coatomic `A` of a finite simple group and `q ∈ π(F(A))`:
`O_q(Z(F(A)))` is a non-trivial subgroup of `A` normalised by `A`, so the coatom/simplicity
argument applies.  (Bender's "hence `C_G(O_q(S)) ≤ A`"; the version of the area lives in
`commutator_pCoreIn_pResidualIn_witness.lean`, which cannot be imported together with the
Dedekind module of this file, so it is reproduced here.) -/
theorem bender17i_centralizer_pCoreIn_zcenterIn_le_coatom {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G]
    (hG : IsSimpleGroup G) (A : Subgroup G) (hA : IsCoatom A) (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime)
    (hqπ : q ∈ Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) :
    Subgroup.centralizer
      ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) : Subgroup G) :
        Set G) ≤ A := by
  have hbot : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≠ ⊥ :=
    Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_zcenterIn_fittingIn_ne_bot A q hq hqπ
  have hNA : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤ A :=
    (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q _).trans
      ((Work.GW2.zcenterIn_le _).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_self A))
  have hnorm : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer
      ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) : Subgroup G) :
        Set G) :=
    Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn_zcenterIn_fittingIn A q
  exact Work.BMAX.le_coatom_of_le_normalizer_of_ne_bot hG hA hbot hNA hnorm
    (Subgroup.centralizer_le_normalizer _)

/-- **Bender 1970, 1.7(i) in the case `E(A) = ⊥`** — proved without the Dedekind auxiliary
`Work.BMAX.Bender17i_fitting_dedekind_hnot`: the whole Thompson argument goes through with the
witness `S = N_{F*(A)}(X)` in place of `F*(A)`, and the coatom argument uses
`O^q(Z(F(A))) ≠ ⊥` (which follows from `hnot` and `E(A) = ⊥`) instead of Dedekind-ness. -/
theorem bender17i_of_layerIn_eq_bot (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (hG : IsSimpleGroup G)
    (A B : Subgroup G) (hA : IsCoatom A) (hB : B ≠ ⊤) (hrel : Work.GW2.BRel A B)
    (hnot : ¬ ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ IsPGroup p (Work.GW2.fstarIn A))
    (hL : Work.GW2.layerIn A = ⊥) :
    Work.GW2.fittingPiIn (Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) B ≤ A := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨X, hX, hXB⟩ := hrel
  set S : Subgroup G := Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) ⊓ Work.GW2.fstarIn A with hSdef
  have hSf : S ≤ Work.GW2.fstarIn A := inf_le_right
  have hSB : S ≤ B := hXB
  -- witness facts: `E(A) ≤ S` and `Z(F(A)) ≤ S`
  have hlayer : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) :=
    le_trans (LayerCentralizesFitting G A) (centralizer_le_normalizer_of_le hX)
  have hzcen : Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) :=
    le_trans (zcenterIn_le_centralizer (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))
      (centralizer_le_normalizer_of_le hX)
  have hZS : Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤ S :=
    le_inf hzcen ((Work.GW2.zcenterIn_le _).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_fstarIn A))
  haveI hFnil : Group.IsNilpotent ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A) := Work.BMAX.isNilpotent_fittingIn A
  set π : Set ℕ := Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) with hπ
  refine le_trans (Work.BMAX.fittingPiIn_le_iSup_pCoreIn B π ?_) ?_
  · intro q hq
    exact Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hq
  · refine iSup_le fun q => iSup_le fun hqπ => ?_
    have hq : q.Prime := Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hqπ
    haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
    -- the two Thompson inputs
    have hD := bender17i_hD_of_layerIn_eq_bot (A := A) (B := B) (S := S) hSB hSf hL q hq
    have hN₀B : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤ B :=
      (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q _).trans (hZS.trans hSB)
    have hN₀S : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤
        Subgroup.centralizer (S : Set G) :=
      (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q _).trans (bender17i_zcenterIn_le_centralizer hSf)
    have hcent : Subgroup.centralizer
        ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) : Subgroup G) : Set G) ≤ A :=
      Work.BMAX.bender17i_centralizer_pCoreIn_zcenterIn_le_coatom hG A hA q hq hqπ
    have hcomm := bender17i_commutator_of_coatom_facts A B S q hq hN₀B hN₀S hcent hSB hD
    -- `O_q(B) ≤ A` via the non-trivial normal subgroup `O^q(Z(F(A)))` of the coatom `A`
    have hQle : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤
        Subgroup.centralizer ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
      Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer.mp hcomm
    set N : Subgroup G := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))
      with hNdef
    have hNS : N ≤ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.mono hZS
    have hNA : N ≤ A := (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le _).trans
      ((Work.GW2.zcenterIn_le _).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_self A))
    have hAN : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (N : Set G) :=
      Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pResidualIn_of_le_normalizer
        (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_zcenterIn_of_le_normalizer (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A))
    have hNne : N ≠ ⊥ := by
      intro hbot
      have hqZ : IsPGroup q ↥(Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) :=
        (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn_eq_bot_iff_isPGroup (p := q)
          (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))).mp hbot
      have hqC : IsPGroup q ↥(Subgroup.center ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) :=
        (Work.BMAX.isPGroup_zcenterIn_iff (K := Work.GW2.fittingIn A) (p := q)).mp hqZ
      have hqF : IsPGroup q ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
        Work.BMAX.isPGroup_of_isPGroup_center_of_isNilpotent hqC
      refine hnot ⟨q, hq, ?_⟩
      rw [Work.GW2.fstarIn_eq_sup, hL, sup_bot_eq]
      exact hqF
    have hQN : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (N : Set G) :=
      hQle.trans ((Subgroup.centralizer_le (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hNS)).trans
        (Subgroup.centralizer_le_normalizer (N : Set G)))
    exact Work.BMAX.le_coatom_of_le_normalizer_of_ne_bot hG hA hNne hNA hAN hQN

/-! ## The general assembly: `hD` for the witness implies Bender 17(i)

The two case lemmas above (`bender17i_hD_of_layerIn_eq_bot` and the companion
`Work.BMAX.Bender17i_hD_of_layerIn_ne_bot`) are exactly the two halves of the missing step

  `hD`:  `⁅O_q(B) ⊓ A, O^q(S)⁆ = ⊥`  for the witness `S = N_{F*(A)}(X)` of `A ⇝ B`,

and with `hD` in hand the whole of Bender 1970, 1.7(i) follows by the Thompson route of
`bender17i_of_layerIn_eq_bot`, with the final coatom argument run on

* `O^q(Z(F(A)))` when that is non-trivial, and
* `E(A) = O^q(E(A))` otherwise (then `Z(F(A))` is a `q`-group, so `F(A)` is a `q`-group and
  `hnot` forces `E(A) ≠ ⊥`).

Note that this assembly (unlike `bender17i_step_fstar_le`) uses **no** Dedekind input. -/
theorem bender17i_of_hD {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] (hG : IsSimpleGroup G)
    (A B X : Subgroup G) (hA : IsCoatom A) (hB : B ≠ ⊤) (hX : X ≤ Work.GW2.fittingIn A)
    (hXB : Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) ⊓ Work.GW2.fstarIn A ≤ B)
    (hnot : ¬ ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ IsPGroup p (Work.GW2.fstarIn A))
    (hD : ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime →
      ⁅Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A,
        Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) ⊓ Work.GW2.fstarIn A)⁆ = ⊥) :
    Work.GW2.fittingPiIn (Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) B ≤ A := by
  classical
  set S : Subgroup G := Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) ⊓ Work.GW2.fstarIn A with hSdef
  have hSf : S ≤ Work.GW2.fstarIn A := inf_le_right
  have hSB : S ≤ B := hXB
  have hlayer : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) :=
    le_trans (LayerCentralizesFitting G A) (centralizer_le_normalizer_of_le hX)
  have hSl : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ S :=
    le_inf hlayer (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_fstarIn A)
  have hzcen : Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) :=
    le_trans (zcenterIn_le_centralizer (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))
      (centralizer_le_normalizer_of_le hX)
  have hZS : Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) ≤ S :=
    le_inf hzcen ((Work.GW2.zcenterIn_le _).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_fstarIn A))
  haveI hFnil : Group.IsNilpotent ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A) := Work.BMAX.isNilpotent_fittingIn A
  set π : Set ℕ := Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) with hπ
  refine le_trans (Work.BMAX.fittingPiIn_le_iSup_pCoreIn B π ?_) ?_
  · intro q hq
    exact Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hq
  · refine iSup_le fun q => iSup_le fun hqπ => ?_
    have hq : q.Prime := Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hqπ
    haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
    have hDq := hD q hq
    have hN₀B : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤ B :=
      (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q _).trans (hZS.trans hSB)
    have hN₀S : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) ≤
        Subgroup.centralizer (S : Set G) :=
      (Work.BMAX.pcpc_pCoreIn_le_self q _).trans (bender17i_zcenterIn_le_centralizer hSf)
    have hcent : Subgroup.centralizer
        ((Work.GW2.pCoreIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) : Subgroup G) : Set G) ≤ A :=
      Work.BMAX.bender17i_centralizer_pCoreIn_zcenterIn_le_coatom hG A hA q hq hqπ
    have hcomm := bender17i_commutator_of_coatom_facts A B S q hq hN₀B hN₀S hcent hSB hDq
    have hQle : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤
        Subgroup.centralizer ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
      Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer.mp hcomm
    by_cases hNbot : Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) = ⊥
    · -- `Z(F(A))` is a `q`-group, so `F(A)` is a `q`-group and `hnot` forces `E(A) ≠ ⊥`:
      -- the coatom argument is run on `E(A) = O^q(E(A))`.
      have hqZ : IsPGroup q ↥(Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) :=
        (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn_eq_bot_iff_isPGroup (p := q)
          (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))).mp hNbot
      have hqC : IsPGroup q ↥(Subgroup.center ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) :=
        (Work.BMAX.isPGroup_zcenterIn_iff (K := Work.GW2.fittingIn A) (p := q)).mp hqZ
      have hqF : IsPGroup q ↥(Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
        Work.BMAX.isPGroup_of_isPGroup_center_of_isNilpotent hqC
      have hEne : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≠ ⊥ := by
        intro hLbot
        refine hnot ⟨q, hq, ?_⟩
        rw [Work.GW2.fstarIn_eq_sup, hLbot, sup_bot_eq]
        exact hqF
      have hEle : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S :=
        (Work.BMAX.pcl_layerIn_le_pResidualIn_self A q hq).trans
          (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.mono hSl)
      have hEA : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ A := Work.GW2.layerIn_le_self A
      have hAEl : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer ((Work.GW2.layerIn A : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
        Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_layerIn A
      have hQN : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤ Subgroup.normalizer ((Work.GW2.layerIn A : Subgroup G) :
          Set G) :=
        hQle.trans ((Subgroup.centralizer_le (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hEle)).trans
          (Subgroup.centralizer_le_normalizer _))
      exact Work.BMAX.le_coatom_of_le_normalizer_of_ne_bot hG hA hEne hEA hAEl hQN
    · -- `O^q(Z(F(A))) ≠ ⊥`: the coatom argument is run on it.
      set N : Subgroup G := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.zcenterIn (Work.GW2.fittingIn A))
        with hNdef
      have hNS : N ≤ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.mono hZS
      have hNA : N ≤ A := (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le _).trans
        ((Work.GW2.zcenterIn_le _).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_self A))
      have hAN : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (N : Set G) :=
        Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pResidualIn_of_le_normalizer
          (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_zcenterIn_of_le_normalizer (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A))
      have hQN : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (N : Set G) :=
        hQle.trans ((Subgroup.centralizer_le (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hNS)).trans
          (Subgroup.centralizer_le_normalizer (N : Set G)))
      exact Work.BMAX.le_coatom_of_le_normalizer_of_ne_bot hG hA hNbot hNA hAN hQN

/-! ## The general `hD`, and the target without any Dedekind input

The missing step of Bender's own proof of 1970, 1.7(ii) is

  `hD`:  `⁅O_q(B) ⊓ A, O^q(S)⁆ = ⊥`  for `S` with `S ≤ B`, `S ≤ F*(A)`, `E(A) ≤ S`

(the witness `S = N_{F*(A)}(X)` of `A ⇝ B` has all three properties).  Here it is proved in
full, with no hypothesis on `E(A)` and **no Dedekind input**, by decomposing a `q'`-element
`x ∈ S` along `O^q(F*(A)) = O^q(F(A)) ⊔ E(A)`:

* `O_q(B) ⊓ A` is solvable and `E(A)`-invariant, so it centralises `E(A)`
  (`layerIn_le_centralizer_of_solvable`);
* writing `x = f·e` with `f ∈ O^q(F(A))`, `e ∈ E(A)` (both `∈ B`, since `x ∈ S ⊆ B` and
  `E(A) ≤ S`), one has `⁅v, x⁆ = ⁅v, f⁆` for `v ∈ O_q(B) ⊓ A` (as `v` centralises `e`), and
  `⁅v, f⁆ ∈ (O_q(B) ⊓ A) ⊓ F(A) ∩ O^q(F(A)) ≤ O_q(A) ⊓ O^q(F(A)) = ⊥`.

This makes `Bender17i` complete: the assembly `bender17i_of_hD` needs nothing else. -/

/-- Every element of `O^q(F*(A))` is a product `f·e` with `f ∈ O^q(F(A))` and `e ∈ E(A)`.

This is the `sSup`-decomposition of `O^q(F*(A)) = O^q(F(A)) ⊔ E(A)` (`pResidualIn_fstarIn_eq_sup`)
carried out inside the group `↥F*(A)`, where both factors are normal. -/
theorem bender17i_decomp_pResidualIn_fstarIn {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G]
    {A : Subgroup G} {q : ℕ} (hq : q.Prime) {x : G}
    (hx : x ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)) :
    ∃ f ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A), ∃ e ∈ Work.GW2.layerIn A, f * e = x := by
  classical
  haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
  have hxFs : x ∈ Work.GW2.fstarIn A := (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le _) hx
  -- `E(A)` viewed in `↥F*(A)` is normal
  have hE'n : ((Work.GW2.layerIn A).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).Normal := by
    rw [Subgroup.normal_subgroupOf_iff_le_normalizer (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_fstarIn A)]
    exact le_trans (Work.GW2.fstarIn_le_self A) (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_layerIn A)
  -- the decomposition `O^q(F*(A)) = O^q(F(A)) ⊔ E(A)` inside `↥F*(A)`
  have hF_map : ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).subgroupOf
        (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).map (Work.GW2.fstarIn A).subtype
      = Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
    Subgroup.map_subgroupOf_eq_of_le
      ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).trans (Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_fstarIn A))
  have hE_map : ((Work.GW2.layerIn A).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).map
        (Work.GW2.fstarIn A).subtype = Work.GW2.layerIn A :=
    Subgroup.map_subgroupOf_eq_of_le (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_fstarIn A)
  have hS_map : ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).subgroupOf
        (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).map (Work.GW2.fstarIn A).subtype
      = Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fstarIn A) :=
    Subgroup.map_subgroupOf_eq_of_le (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le _)
  have hsup : (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A) ⊔
        (Work.GW2.layerIn A).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)
      = (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A) := by
    refine Subgroup.map_injective (Subgroup.subtype_injective (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)) ?_
    rw [Subgroup.map_sup, hF_map, hE_map, hS_map, Work.BMAX.pResidualIn_fstarIn_eq_sup A hq]
  have hx' : (⟨x, hxFs⟩ : ↥(Work.GW2.fstarIn A)) ∈
      (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A) :=
    Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mpr hx
  rw [← hsup] at hx'
  haveI : ((Work.GW2.layerIn A).subgroupOf (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)).Normal := hE'n
  obtain ⟨f, hf, e, he, hfe⟩ := Subgroup.mem_sup_of_normal_right.mp hx'
  exact ⟨f.1, Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mp hf, e.1, Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mp he,
    congrArg Subtype.val hfe⟩

/-- **The step `hD` of Bender 1970, 1.7(ii)**, in full generality: if `S ≤ B`, `S ≤ F*(A)` and
`E(A) ≤ S`, then `O_q(B) ⊓ A` commutes with `O^q(S)`. -/
theorem bender17i_hD {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] {A B S : Subgroup G}
    (hSB : S ≤ B) (hSf : S ≤ Work.GW2.fstarIn A) (hSl : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ S)
    (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime) :
    ⁅Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A, Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S⁆ = ⊥ := by
  classical
  haveI : Fact q.Prime := ⟨hq⟩
  set V : Subgroup G := Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B ⊓ A with hVdef
  -- `V` is solvable and `E(A)`-invariant, hence centralised by `E(A)`
  have hVE : V ≤ Subgroup.centralizer ((Work.GW2.layerIn A : Subgroup G) : Set G) := by
    haveI : Group.IsNilpotent ↥V :=
      ((Work.BMAX.pcpc_isPGroup_pCoreIn q B).to_le inf_le_left).isNilpotent
    have hsol : Group.IsSolvable ↥V := IsNilpotent.to_isSolvable
    have hLn : V ≤ Subgroup.normalizer ((Work.GW2.layerIn A : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
      (inf_le_right : V ≤ A).trans (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_layerIn A)
    have hEn : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (V : Set G) := by
      rw [Subgroup.le_normalizer_iff]
      intro e he y hy
      obtain ⟨hyQ, hyA⟩ := Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hy
      refine Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · exact (Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp
          (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn B q (hSB (hSl he))) y).mp hyQ
      · exact A.mul_mem (A.mul_mem (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_self A he) hyA)
          (A.inv_mem (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_self A he))
    exact Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff.mp (Work.BMAX.layerIn_le_centralizer_of_solvable hsol hLn hEn)
  rw [Subgroup.commutator_eq_bot_iff_le_centralizer]
  refine (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff (H := V)
    (K := Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q S)).mpr ?_
  rw [Work.BMAX.pResidualIn]
  refine (Subgroup.closure_le (K := Subgroup.centralizer (V : Set G))).mpr ?_
  rintro x ⟨hxS, hxq⟩
  -- decompose `x` along `O^q(F*(A)) = O^q(F(A)) ⊔ E(A)`
  obtain ⟨f, hf, e, he, hfe⟩ := bender17i_decomp_pResidualIn_fstarIn (A := A) hq
    (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.subset_closure (hSf hxS) hxq)
  have hfF : f ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A := (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn.le _) hf
  have hfA : f ∈ A := Work.GW2.fittingIn_le_self A hfF
  have heB : e ∈ B := hSB (hSl he)
  have hfB : f ∈ B := by
    have hfeq : f = x * e⁻¹ := by rw [← hfe]; group
    rw [hfeq]
    exact B.mul_mem (hSB hxS) (B.inv_mem heB)
  refine Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mpr ?_
  intro v hv
  obtain ⟨hvQ, hvA⟩ := Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hv
  -- `⁅v, f⁆ = 1`
  have hconjQ : f * v * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B :=
    (Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pCoreIn B q hfB) v).mp hvQ
  have hfinvQ : f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B := by
    have h := (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B).inv_mem hconjQ
    rwa [show (f * v * f⁻¹)⁻¹ = f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ from by group] at h
  have hcomQ : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B := by
    have h := (Work.GW2.pCoreIn q B).mul_mem hvQ hfinvQ
    rwa [show v * (f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹) = v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ from by group] at h
  have hcomA : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ A :=
    A.mul_mem (A.mul_mem (A.mul_mem hvA hfA) (A.inv_mem hvA)) (A.inv_mem hfA)
  have hconjF : v * f * v⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A :=
    (Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A hvA) f).mp hfF
  have hcomF : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.fittingIn A :=
    (Work.GW2.fittingIn A).mul_mem hconjF ((Work.GW2.fittingIn A).inv_mem hfF)
  have hOqA : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.GW2.pCoreIn q A :=
    Work.BMAX.inf_fittingIn_le_pCoreIn_of_le_pCoreIn A B V q hq inf_le_left inf_le_right
      (Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hcomQ, hcomA⟩, hcomF⟩)
  have hAR : A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer
      ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
    Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_pResidualIn_of_le_normalizer (Work.BMAX.le_normalizer_fittingIn A)
  have hOqR : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) :=
    (Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).mul_mem
      ((Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff.mp (hAR hvA) f).mp hf)
      ((Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)).inv_mem hf)
  have hvf1 : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ = 1 := by
    have hinf : Work.GW2.pCoreIn q A ⊓
        Work.BMAX.pResidualIn q (Work.GW2.fittingIn A) = ⊥ :=
      Work.BMAX.pCoreIn_inf_pResidualIn_fittingIn_eq_bot A q hq
    have : v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹ ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup G) := by
      rw [← hinf]
      exact Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hOqA, hOqR⟩
    exact Subgroup.mem_bot.mp this
  have hvf : v * f = f * v := by
    calc v * f = (v * f * v⁻¹ * f⁻¹) * (f * v) := by group
      _ = f * v := by rw [hvf1, one_mul]
  -- `⁅v, e⁆ = 1`, hence `⁅v, f·e⁆ = 1`
  have hve : v * e = e * v := ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp (hVE hv)) e he).symm
  show v * x = x * v
  rw [← hfe]
  calc v * (f * e) = (v * f) * e := by group
    _ = (f * v) * e := by rw [hvf]
    _ = f * (v * e) := by group
    _ = f * (e * v) := by rw [hve]
    _ = (f * e) * v := by group

/-- **Bender 1970, 1.7(i).**  Assembled from `bender17i_of_hD` with the general step `hD`
(`bender17i_hD`) run on the witness `S = N_{F*(A)}(X)` of the relation `A ⇝ B`: Bender's own
Thompson argument, with **no** Dedekind input and **no** hypothesis on `E(A)`. -/
theorem Bender17i (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (hG : IsSimpleGroup G) (A B : Subgroup G)
    (hA : IsCoatom A) (hB : B ≠ ⊤) (hrel : Work.GW2.BRel A B)
    (hnot : ¬ ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ IsPGroup p (Work.GW2.fstarIn A)) :
    Work.GW2.fittingPiIn (Work.GW2.primesOf (Work.GW2.fittingIn A)) B ≤ A := by
  obtain ⟨X, hX, hXB⟩ := hrel
  have hSl : Work.GW2.layerIn A ≤ Subgroup.normalizer (X : Set G) ⊓ Work.GW2.fstarIn A :=
    le_inf (le_trans (LayerCentralizesFitting G A) (centralizer_le_normalizer_of_le hX))
      (Work.GW2.layerIn_le_fstarIn A)
  exact bender17i_of_hD hG A B X hA hB hX hXB hnot
    (fun q hq => bender17i_hD hXB inf_le_right hSl q hq)

end Work.BMAX
